PQDIF normative definitions
============================

The PQDIF writer in pqdif_converter.cpp uses the subset of standard tags,
record identifiers, semantic identifiers, physical types, and physical-record
layout needed by this implementation. Those definitions were transcribed from
the IEEE SA Open `pqdif/pqdif-normative` project, release 1.0.0, commit
7119d2ac27841da5bc41fbe1484b82b2d3f84f11:

https://opensource.ieee.org/pqdif/pqdif-normative/-/tree/1.0.0

The upstream definitions are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The complete license text is retained in this repository's top-level LICENSE.
No upstream implementation code is installed on the target, and no IEEE or
third-party vendor identity is emitted as the recording-device vendor.
